# A chat's photo message is a focusable frame around the picture, and the app opens its viewer only for a click on the picture itself, so Enter on the frame did nothing. Enter clicks the picture, as a mouse would; a small avatar in a text message is not taken for the message.
pages/photo-message.html
start:css=#photo
key:Enter
wait:200
eval:(() => { const t = document.getElementById('view').textContent; if (t !== 'Viewer: photo') throw new Error(t); return t; })()
key:ArrowDown
expect:css=#note
key:Enter
wait:200
eval:(() => { const t = document.getElementById('view').textContent; if (t !== 'Opened: message') throw new Error(t); return t; })()
